  ==> kappa_B = 0.58 +/- 0.18   (R1; dominated by the BULGE mass-to-light ratio; the repository's 0.551 +/- 0.043 held Ups_bul fixed at 0.7 on the tabulated distances; tabulated centre 0.547)
  a common distance rescaling of 5 and 10 per cent moves the shape-only a0 by 9.8e-12 (fractional) and the standard fit by 22.5% (10 per cent case)
  bulgeless galaxies only (132 galaxies, 1715 points, g_bar < 16 a0): kappa_B = 0.51, 0.78, 1.13 at Ups_disc = 0.5, 0.6, 0.7  -> the lever arm is too short; no help
  deep band g_bar < 0.1 a0 (bulge 0.7): kappa = 0.505 (N 858), 0.444 (N 764), 0.397 (N 688) at Upsilon_disc = 0.5, 0.6, 0.7
     every point, equal weight (no quality cut): 0.403, 0.352, 0.310  <- points with >10% velocity errors pull it down
  injection (a0 = 0.7, 1.0, 1.3 x canonical, real g_bar, noise = quoted errors + 0.034 dex): returned / injected
     standard fit 1.004, 1.008, 0.998;  deep band 1.001, 1.021, 1.008
     with a +0.08 dex common offset (a 20% distance error): shape-only 1.023, 1.015, 1.004;  the standard fit, for contrast, 1.662, 1.639, 1.603
  [PASS] [data] S2a REPLICATION: on SPARC's tabulated distances at Upsilon_disc = 0.5 the fit returns the literature a0 = 1.2e-10 within 5%   (a0 = 1.190e-10)
  [PASS] [data] S2a2 the Planck-consistent distances LOWER the standard-fit a0 (the Hubble-flow g_obs fall by 1/1.083): at Upsilon_disc = 0.5 by 5-15 per cent   (1.049e-10 vs 1.190e-10 (-11.9%))
  [PASS] [data] S2b the degeneracy is steep: kappa moves by more than 0.15 between Upsilon_disc = 0.5 and 0.7   (0.560 -> 0.381)
  [PASS] [identity] S2d the shape-only estimator is immune to a common distance rescaling (< 1e-5): the free offset absorbs it by construction   (9.8e-12)
  [PASS] [data] S2d2 while the standard fit is not: a 10 per cent common rescaling moves it by more than 15 per cent   (22.5%)
  [PASS] [identity] S2e on the tabulated distances the replication agrees with the repository's earlier estimator B at Upsilon_bul = 0.7, Upsilon_disc = 0.5 and 0.7 (0.529, 0.574) within 0.01 (code replication)   (0.528, 0.573)
  [PASS] [data] S2f AGAINST THE EARLIER ERROR BAR: the bulge mass-to-light ratio moves estimator B by more than twice the 0.043 previously quoted   (bulge term 0.124; total 0.184)
  [PASS] [data] S2g restricting the fit to the deep band (g_bar < 0.1 a0, quality-cut, error-weighted) does NOT remove the mass-to-light dependence: kappa moves by more than 0.08 across Upsilon_disc 0.5-0.7   (0.505, 0.444, 0.397)
  [PASS] [data] S2h AGAINST INTEREST: giving every deep point equal weight (no quality cut) lowers kappa by at least 0.05 at every Upsilon   (0.403, 0.352, 0.310)
  [PASS] [injection] I1 the standard fit returns the injected a0 to 2 per cent at 0.7, 1.0 and 1.3 x canonical   (1.004, 1.008, 0.998)
  [PASS] [injection] I2 the shape-only estimator returns the injected a0 to 3 per cent through a 0.08 dex common offset that biases the standard fit by > 15 per cent   (shape 1.023, 1.015, 1.004; standard 1.662, 1.639, 1.603)
  [PASS] [injection] I3 the deep-band fit returns the injected a0 to 5 per cent   (1.001, 1.021, 1.008)
  [PASS] [data] S2c kappa = 1/2 needs a disc mass-to-light ratio inside the population-synthesis range 0.4-0.8   (0.55 / 0.47)
  estimator A: correction evaluated at the canonical a0 8.7091e-11; at its own output (fixed point) 8.6533e-11 (-0.64%); selection and correction at the 21% higher alternative a0 9.5263e-11 (+9.4%); total error 16.24%
  [PASS] [data] S2i estimator A is not an echo of the a0 at which its correction is evaluated: iterating to its own output moves it by < 1 per cent, and a 21 per cent change of that a0 moves it by < 10 per cent (a sensitivity test on the real data)   (-0.64%, +9.4%)
  H0-convention audit: q_HF = 0.202;  estimator A box: R1 0.4504, MIXED 0.4651, R2a 0.4294, R2b 0.4156  (audit prints MIXED 0.4652, R1 0.4503, R2a 0.4295, R2b 0.4155)
  ==> estimator A (R1) kappa = 0.450 +/- 0.073   [tabulated distances: 0.465 +/- 0.076]
  [PASS] [identity] S3e estimator A's convention box reproduces the repository audit (R1, MIXED, R2a, R2b) to 0.002, with the paper's H0 = 67.4 in place of the audit's 67.36   (R1 0.4504/0.4503, MIXED 0.4651/0.4652, R2a 0.4294/0.4295, R2b 0.4156/0.4155)

